WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.510
- What were your like pop
culture, obsessions, growing up?

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.350
- I didn't really have any.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.703
I just loved Star Wars
and Lord of the Rings.

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:12.101
- So you're sci-fi, all right!

00:00:12.101 --> 00:00:15.000
- Yeah, but I wasn't
like, obsessed with them.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.690
People were obsessed with the Spice Girls

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:17.650
when I was growing up

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.160
and I would attend
these Spice Girl parties

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.470
and do the thing and dress up.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.740
And I was Sporty Spice
because I played sports,

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:27.970
so it was one I could understand the most.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.820
And then we had to do these
music videos, you know,

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.050
fake music videos at friends' birthdays,

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.530
and I don't know any of the words.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:36.400
And I just,

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.540
everyone had an obsession as a child

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:39.840
and I feel like I didn't.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.350
And I feel like I've
lost out on something.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.430
- No, it's so funny.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.270
So right whenever I got in the industry,

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.070
I would have to go on
TRL and all the video,

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:50.170
like I didn't have, we had
like the basic eight channels.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.820
So I didn't really know about pop culture

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.510
because we were poor.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.170
Like, and we didn't, I
didn't read magazines.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:56.500
We didn't have the internet
like how we have it now,

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.333
whenever I was little.

00:00:57.333 --> 00:00:58.750
So I just didn't know.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.387
And like, I remember being
on TRL and they'll be like,

00:01:00.387 --> 00:01:01.590
"What are your favorite videos?"

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:05.287
And you're trying not to offend
MTV, but I didn't see one!

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.847
And I was trying to ask
the person over here,

00:01:08.847 --> 00:01:10.140
"What was your favorite?"

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.030
You know, which one I loved.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.200
And then I'd just say whatever they said.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.830
So I wasn't really that into it either.

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:15.970
I was very creative on my own,

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:16.820
were you kind of that kid,

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.490
that kind of just did whatever?

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:19.400
I played sports as well.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.790
Were you that kid that
beat to your own drum?

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.280
- Yes.
- Yeah.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.770
- I was an athlete and I was a dancer

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:29.700
and I was obsessed with
whatever thing I was practicing,

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:32.770
but you brought up MTV and it,

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:34.940
I just need to let you know that we went,

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:37.760
my fiance and I went
down a big rabbit hole

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:40.830
of you on MTV and on SNL

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.817
singing Since You've Been Gone.

00:01:42.817 --> 00:01:44.570
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.570
It is, we just like,

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:49.270
couldn't stop watching
old videos of you singing.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:50.103
They're just,

00:01:50.103 --> 00:01:54.410
it's so phenomenal and emotional
and made us cry every time.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:55.243
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:55.243 --> 00:01:57.110
- Such great vintage MTV,

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.650
not vintage because it
was like 10 years ago.

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:00.640
- No it wasn't, it's vintage!

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.473
And what's crazy though,

00:02:01.473 --> 00:02:02.610
is you'll experience this in your life,

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:04.920
you'll have done a project years ago,

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.010
which you probably have already,

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:06.843
and you're like,

00:02:06.843 --> 00:02:08.900
it's such a different
chapter of your life.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.110
It's like different chapters in your book

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:14.960
and it's cool, but it's good
to make sure you slow down,

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.990
'cause I think I'm quite
a bit older than you,

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:18.100
I'm like at least a decade.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.110
And I think it's good to like slow down

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:21.960
and enjoy all those moments.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.980
'cause sometimes I didn't
because you're always worried

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.515
about your next project or
your next thing, but yeah,

00:02:26.515 --> 00:02:28.977
I do remember getting to
trash a whole apartment

00:02:28.977 --> 00:02:30.555
in that video, which was cool.

00:02:30.555 --> 00:02:32.665
I was like, "I get paid to do this?"

00:02:32.665 --> 00:02:35.740
So what about, what about a
favorite classic sitcom though?

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.510
Because you have so many sitcoms,

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:38.410
I feel like they're pulling

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:39.920
from so many sitcoms for WandaVision.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:42.480
Did you have any, like
I loved, I Love Lucy.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.620
I was obsessed.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.110
Did you love any like classic ones?

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:48.130
- I loved Laverne and Shirley,

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:51.290
but I grew up with like the nineties ones.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.830
So The Torkelsons was like a,

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:55.270
was a family show

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:58.030
that was really sincere.
- [Kelly] Wait, the what?

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:58.863
- I don't know.

00:02:58.863 --> 00:03:00.980
I, my best friend and I believe

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.470
the mom of The Torkelsons,

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:03.790
'cause we're from the valley,

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:07.330
lived on his street or we
saw her on his street once,

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.070
and it was,

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:12.150
that was like the most exciting
person we could have seen

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.607
because her daughter speaks
to the man in the moon

00:03:14.607 --> 00:03:17.440
and we just, it was, it was very exciting.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:19.370
The Torkelsons was, I don't know.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:20.930
I don't even know if
we liked it ironically

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.550
or if we understood irony at that age,

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.890
but we loved The Torkelsons.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.560
- I'm totally gonna YouTube
that tonight and be like,

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:28.560
what are you talking about?

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:29.710
I've never heard of it.

